"answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative launched by Alex, with Sarah Tan as the lead and a Phase One budget of $500,000. The project kick-off was scheduled for June 15th. In July, Emily called for R&D ideas to leverage AI in data visualization, with proposals due by July 20th. In September, the team expanded by adding five members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with onboarding on September 10th. By October, Carlos announced the successful completion of the testing phase, celebrated on October 10th. In November, Neil reported a breakthrough in predictive analytics during Phase Two, with a detailed report to be shared on November 20th. Additionally, Fiona announced a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research. Regarding resources, Jane Doe (HR) approved a $15,000 budget for coding and project manager training, while Carla noted a $55,000 budget for compliance plan training and audits. Finally, feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought from stakeholders by the end of November."
